  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The refractive index of a medium is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msqrt></math>.</p><p>For medium&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Now speed of light in a medium will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
